  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NULL - Pakistan (01-Jul-2015-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pakistan, Tuberculosis, Mercy Corps (MC)This program has the following goals: Contribute to achieving the goal of the national strategy to control TB in Pakistan which is to reduce by 50% the prevalence of TB by 2025 in comparison to 2011.  Contribute towards decreasing the prevalence, by at least 5% per year from 2018 onwards, the prevalence of MDR-TB among TB patients who have never received any TB treatment. The objectives of this program are: To enhance MDR-TB enrolment from 18% of estimated cases in 2013-14 to 23% of estimated by 2017.  To increase TB case notification (all forms) from 61% of estimated incident cases in 2013-14 to 71% of estimated incident cases by 2017 while maintaining treatment success rate at 91%.  To increase the number of TB patients who are screened for HIV infection from 3% in 2013-14 to 10% by 2017.</narrative>
  </description>
